### Logic Level Shifter

-   Since the Pi uses 3.3 V for communication, and the Arduino 5 V, a
    logic level shifter is needed. These modules are available cheaply
    and two 6-pin female headers should be used as a socket for easy
    install/removal. See FIGURE 29 - DYER ISLAND MONITOR.

-   The level shifter uses the 3.3V on pin 1 of the Raspberry Pi
    connector for the LV connection and the 5V Arduino supply voltage
    for the HV connection.

